<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cleartext is permitted, because remote mode accepts http:// addresses for people who host
  Fava on a home LAN or behind a VPN, where a certificate for 192.168.1.5 is not a realistic
  thing to ask for.

  What this does NOT do is make the app casual about it. The only cleartext requests the app
  ever makes are to 127.0.0.1 (the embedded Fava) and to an address the user typed in full,
  http:// and all. Nothing infers cleartext, nothing falls back to it after an https failure,
  and the remote screen says plainly what an http address means. Local mode still makes no
  network requests at all.

  Certificate handling is unchanged and unrelated: when an address is https, verification is
  strict, a certificate error is fatal, and there is no override anywhere in the app.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
